# Keep the build context to what install.sh actually compiles. Everything the
# Go build needs (go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/, install.sh) is NOT listed.
#
# .git is deliberately kept: install.sh derives the version stamp from
# `git describe`, and dropping it would silently downgrade every local build to
# "dev". Automated builders that copy without history get the same fallback and
# can pass --build-arg RUNECHO_VERSION instead.

# Build and coverage artefacts
coverage.out
*.test
/out
/dist

# Documentation and planning — not compiled, and docs/ is the largest tree here
docs/
plans/
*.md
!README.md

# Local editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Nothing in the image consumes these
.github/
.codegraph/
